<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Koala on Kunal Kushwaha</title><link>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/tags/koala/</link><description>Recent content in Koala on Kunal Kushwaha</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0900</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/tags/koala/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Keep the Agent's Packets Out of the Host Kernel</title><link>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/11/09/keep-agent-packets-out-of-host-kernel/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/11/09/keep-agent-packets-out-of-host-kernel/</guid><description>&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="fig-card"&gt;&lt;img src="hero.png" alt="An AI agent works inside a glass box, its own VM. Its packet travels along a blue path through Koala, a koala at a laptop beside a stack of layers, and out to the globe. A red dashed path from the agent’s box toward a large host server with a glowing core is blocked by a red X at the server’s door." loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;An AI agent works inside a glass box, its own VM. Its packet travels along a blue path through Koala, a koala at a laptop beside a stack of layers, and out to the globe. A red dashed path from the agent’s box toward a large host server with a glowing core is blocked by a red X at the server’s door.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;An autonomous agent with a shell has superpowers. It installs packages, runs scripts, opens connections and fixes its own mistakes, without waiting for anyone. Nobody reviews each command. That&amp;rsquo;s the point.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Before I Trust an Agent, I Try to Break Its Box</title><link>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/11/06/before-i-trust-an-agent/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/11/06/before-i-trust-an-agent/</guid><description>&lt;div class="note"&gt;&lt;span class="note-label"&gt;Updated 15 November 2026 for 0.1.0-rc.3&lt;/span&gt;The attack results below were recorded in October 2026 on Koala&amp;rsquo;s preview builds. This update adds &lt;a href="#leave-it-running-for-eight-hours"&gt;the eight-hour runs&lt;/a&gt; and domain grants from rc.3, and marks the bugs fixed since.&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="fig-card"&gt;&lt;img src="hero.jpg" alt="Untrusted code runs inside the VM. The host stays outside the guest boundary." loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Untrusted code runs inside the VM. The host stays outside the guest boundary.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;An AI agent is not a predictable app. It reads web pages, messages, and files, and it may act on instructions hidden in any of them. The safer assumption is that, sooner or later, something untrusted will run wherever the agent runs.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>A Clean Room Is Not a Home</title><link>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/10/30/a-clean-room-is-not-a-home/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/10/30/a-clean-room-is-not-a-home/</guid><description>&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="fig-card"&gt;&lt;img src="hero.png" alt="A Clean Room Is Not a Home. On the left, an empty glass box with a desk and a checklist. On the right, an agent works in its own lit room in a building, with keys locked in a vault below and every connection to the outside passing through a guarded gate." loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;A Clean Room Is Not a Home. On the left, an empty glass box with a desk and a checklist. On the right, an agent works in its own lit room in a building, with keys locked in a vault below and every connection to the outside passing through a guarded gate.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When I hear &amp;ldquo;sandbox&amp;rdquo; today, the picture is usually a coding agent: a container, a repo, run the tests, throw it away. That works. But an agent that answers email or runs a workflow for months is not a coding agent with a longer timeout. It lives somewhere.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>